## Final Assessment

There was **no known exploitation**, but the discovered configuration represented a high-impact security weakness.

The combination of a **long-lived access key**, **unrestricted IAM permissions**, and the ability to **create persistent administrative access** meant that compromise of a single credential could have resulted in full AWS account compromise.

The remediation does not attempt to eliminate the bootstrap identity prematurely. Instead, it establishes a clear security boundary:

> **The bootstrap credential bootstraps the account. The deployment role operates the account.**

This preserves the practical requirements of initial Terraform provisioning while removing unnecessary administrator privileges from the long-lived credential.
